        "original_id": "7cc958af-a4c1-5781-a185-c90441554614",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: High School (1968 film), The Thorn in the Heart\n- People: Frederick Wiseman, Michel Gondry\n- Places: Northeast High School, Philadelphia, Pennsylvania\n- Concepts: direct cinema, cinéma vérité\n\nFacts:\n- High School is a 1968 American documentary film directed by Frederick Wiseman.\n- High School shows a typical day for a group of students at Northeast High School in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania.\n- High School was shot over five weeks in March and April 1968.\n- High School was one of the first direct cinema, or cinéma vérité, documentaries.\n- The Thorn in the Heart is a 2009 French documentary film directed by Michel Gondry.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
